  <data name="Cli_Help" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>[bold]simple-bike-trainer-cli[/]: rides Intervals.icu workouts on a KICKR CORE 2 with Zwift Click controllers

[bold]simple-bike-trainer-cli ride[/] [grey](the default)[/]
  Pick a planned ride from Intervals.icu (today and the next 6 days), connect, and ride it.
  --event &lt;id&gt;        ride this Intervals.icu event
  --date &lt;yyyy-mm-dd&gt; list rides from this day instead of today
  --free              free ride on the virtual gears
  --ramp              built-in ramp FTP test   --ramp-start &lt;W&gt; (default 100)
  --route &lt;distance&gt;  a generated rolling loop, in km (mi with imperial units)
    [[--climb &lt;m or ft&gt;]] [[--seed &lt;n&gt;]]   its total climbing; the same seed gives the same route
  --file &lt;path&gt;       a workout file: Intervals.icu workout text, or event or workout_doc JSON
  --ftp &lt;W&gt;           override the FTP for this ride
  --offline           do not contact Intervals.icu
  --upload | --no-upload   upload the ride afterward without asking, or never
  --upload-to intervals,garmin   pick the destinations for this ride
  --no-hr, --no-click  skip the heart rate monitor or the Zwift Click
  --simulate          use a simulated trainer and heart rate monitor instead of Bluetooth or ANT+
  --speed &lt;n&gt;         with --simulate, run n times faster
  --no-ui             print a status line every 10 s instead of the dashboard

[bold]simple-bike-trainer-cli scan[/] [[--seconds 15]]   list trainers, heart rate monitors, and Zwift controllers; save the picks
[bold]simple-bike-trainer-cli probe[/] [[--seconds 30]]  connect read-only and print trainer data and Click presses
    [[--control [[--watts 100]]]]   also take control and set ERG power (resets on exit)
    [[--wifi &lt;host[[:port]]&gt;]]   skip the scan and connect to a Wahoo Direct Connect trainer at this address
[bold]simple-bike-trainer-cli workouts[/] [[--days 7]]   list planned rides from Intervals.icu
[bold]simple-bike-trainer-cli upload &lt;file.fit&gt;[/] [[--event &lt;id&gt;]] [[--name &lt;name&gt;]]
[bold]simple-bike-trainer-cli connect garmin[/]   sign in to Garmin Connect (email, password, and MFA code); saves session tokens only
[bold]simple-bike-trainer-cli config[/] [[--api-key K]] [[--athlete-id ID]] [[--ftp W]] [[--units metric|imperial]]
    [[--weight N]] [[--bike-weight N]]   (in kg, or lb with imperial units)   [[--max-hr BPM]]
    [[--upload-to intervals,garmin]] [[--auto-upload true|false]] [[--forget-devices]]   show or change settings
    [[--wifi-trainers host[[:port]],...]]   Wi-Fi trainers to look for at these addresses when the network scan cannot find them
    [[--resistance power|virtual-gears|real-gears]]   off ERG: the app sets the power from virtual gears (power), or the trainer
        simulates the road with virtual gears (virtual-gears) or with the bike's gears (real-gears)
    [[--chain 34x17]]   the chainring and cog on a single-speed setup   [[--crr 0.004]]   the tires' rolling resistance

Settings are saved in ~/.config/simple-bike-trainer/config.json, or %APPDATA%\simple-bike-trainer\config.json on Windows. INTERVALS_API_KEY overrides the saved key.
</value>
    <comment>Spectre.Console markup: keep the [bold] and [grey] tags, and write a literal [ as [[ and ] as ]].</comment>
